## Browser Testing

### Direct image embed
```html
<img src="https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=https://google.com" alt="Google QR">
```

### With custom size
```html
<img src="https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=Hello%20World&size=300" alt="Hello QR" width="300" height="300">
```

### SVG embed
```html
<img src="https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=Test&format=svg" alt="Test QR">
```

---

## Cache Testing

### First request (cache miss)
```bash
curl -v "https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=cache-test-123" --output /dev/null
# Look for: X-Vercel-Cache: MISS
```

### Repeat request (cache hit)
```bash
curl -v "https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=cache-test-123" --output /dev/null
# Look for: X-Vercel-Cache: HIT
```

### Check cache headers
```bash
curl -I "https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=cache-test-123"
# Should show: Cache-Control: public, s-maxage=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
```

---

## QR Code Verification

### Using zbarimg (Linux)
```bash
# Install: sudo apt install zbar-tools
curl "https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=https://google.com" --output test.png
zbarimg test.png
```

### Using Python
```python
# pip install pyzbar pillow
from pyzbar import pyzbar
from PIL import Image

img = Image.open("test.png")
decoded = pyzbar.decode(img)
print(decoded[0].data.decode())
```

### Online verification
Upload generated PNG to: https://zxing.org/w/decode.jspx

---

## Load Testing (lightweight)

### Quick concurrent test
```bash
for i in {1..10}; do
  curl -s "https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=load-test-$i" --output /dev/null &
done
wait
```

### With timing
```bash
for i in {1..5}; do
  time curl -s "https://qr.tomaseu.pw/qr?text=timing-test-$i" --output /dev/null
done
```